  "description": "An element access whose index the compiler types as a literal type or a union of them references each member those literals name, as a read or a write. An index that is an unassigned keyof parameter of a function whose every call the target holds is decided at the calls, by each argument's type or by the parameter's default, so a member no call passes stays reported. Where the function escapes as a value or is reached through an interface, the access reads every member its index type admits. A non-generic parameter typed by keyof of a type parameter reads the member a literal argument names.",
